# public_eval_7491f3cf — current authoring design

The frame contains four equal panels. In panel one, the largest 8-connected guide
component is a separating wall and the isolated guide cell marks one side. Panel
two supplies the marker-side region, panel three supplies the other side, and
panel-two foreground wins on wall cells. This reproduces all four train labels
and the private-gold test label.

Native parameter `marker_panel=second|third` swaps the two source roles while
retaining the same guide inference. The intermediate is the flooded marker-side
region; per-cell composition cannot be chosen before that mask exists. Fresh
lessons vary wall topology, marker side, colors, overlaps and layout, including
a four-panel 30x30 query. Owner registration and acceptance remain pending.
